  "id": "reactive-depression",
  "term": "reactive depression",
  "definition": "Reactive depression is a subtype of depression that begins after a significant stressor or severe life event. It describes a depressed state understood as being triggered by environmental circumstances, in contrast to depression occurring without an identifiable stress-related trigger.",
